Pattern sources
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Wikipedia-derived pattern catalogs and associated adaptations in both
humanizer skills are distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Their upstream MIT notices
also remain included; the plugin-level MIT license does not override share-alike
terms on this material. Full text: licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt.

Source: Wikipedia, "Signs of AI writing", by Wikipedia contributors, including
WikiProject AI Cleanup. Attribution and contributor history:
  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Signs_of_AI_writing
  https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Wikipedia:Signs_of_AI_writing&action=history
Upstream did not identify an exact source revision. No endorsement is implied.
Changes here: catalogs extracted into references; navigation and attribution added;
Taiwan-specific instructional prose translated into en-US while preserving
language examples. New System One instructions are separately identified in the
skills. Keep this attribution and license when redistributing adapted catalogs.

Namespace and language modifications: all packaged skill names and directories use
the s1- prefix. Instructions use en-US; protected target-language examples and
upstream copyright names remain unchanged. Review guidance now requires grounded
smells and checked runtime claims; grilling recommendations must identify unknown
cost/capacity assumptions and leave them marked as unknown.
